          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How many amps does a well pump draw?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "At 240 volts, a 1/2 HP pump typically draws around 4 to 6 amps running, a 3/4 HP pump around 6 to 8, a 1 HP pump around 8 to 10 and a 1.5 HP pump around 10 to 13. Starting current is several times higher for a moment. The control box or motor nameplate lists the exact full-load amps for your pump."
          }
