          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do I need a transfer switch for a well pump generator?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, or an interlock kit with a power inlet. A well pump is hardwired on a 240V double-pole circuit, so the only safe way to power it from a generator is through transfer equipment installed by a licensed electrician. Never backfeed through a dryer outlet with a double-male cord, which can electrocute utility workers."
          }
