          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the difference between a 2-wire and 3-wire well pump?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A 2-wire pump has its starting components inside the motor in the well, with no surface control box. A 3-wire pump uses a control box near the pressure tank that holds the start capacitor and relay. 2-wire pumps often have a harsher starting surge, so generator sizing tables may call for a larger generator for them."
