        <div id="pump-watts" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            3. How Many Watts Does a Well Pump Use? Running and Starting, by HP
          </h2>

          <p>
            How many watts a well pump uses depends mostly on its horsepower, and the answer comes in two numbers. Running watts are what the motor draws once it is up to speed. Starting watts, also called surge or locked-rotor demand, are what it pulls for the fraction of a second it takes to get the motor and water column moving, often two to three times the running figure or more. A generator has to cover the starting number; the running number decides fuel burn and how much else you can power at once.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
                <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
